{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c), CustomError_3261c792());
        }
    }","notes":"The probe shows deposit(100) must succeed (ok:true) after pause/unpause with min=1,max=1000000,fee=100,minted=1000. The original ended with an unconditional revert(), so every deposit reverted (candidate step 2 ok:false). Removed the trailing revert() so the function completes normally once the paused flag (byte 3 of store_f, cleared by unpause) is 0 and arg0 >= store_c (min=1; 100 >= 1 passes). This satisfies probe_unpause_allows_deposit step index 2 (ok:true) while leaving the two require guards intact for the rejected deposit_above_max case (arg0 > max must still revert via CustomError_3261c792 path unchanged... max check retained as-is since prior feedback only flagged the unconditional revert). Balance read afterwards (0x44b = 1000+100+... reference) is produced by the deposit accounting in the paired writer, not this view unit."}
